      ":question/problem": "![](images/63/63c01809e44e6b6dff42974578ec96363abd70ebaae9cb031a0823dbf892140f.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curves $y = 2x^{2} - 4x + 1$ and $y = 2x + 1$, as shown in the picture. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are rectangles. If the height of each rectangle is $3$ times the length of its base, which integral gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
